  "docTrailer": "# ADR-014: Invoices are immutable after issuance\n\n## Context\n\nFinance/audit systems assume issued invoices are an append-only record.\nMutating an issued invoice (e.g. to correct a typo) would break reconciliation\nwith downstream ledgers.\n\n## Decision\n\n- `Invoice.issuedAt` is set exactly once; we never re-issue.\n- Corrections are modelled as **credit notes** (a separate aggregate),\n  not as mutations.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `Invoice` has no setters beyond the initial constructor pathway.\n- The domain service rejects any command whose target has `issuedAt != null`."
